      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Misinterpretation of reversible defects at the base of the interventricular septum is perhaps among the greatest single causes of false positive TI-201 myocardial perfusion images. This is a report of a patient with angiographically documented ischemia at the base of the septum and corresponding reversible defects as seen using TI-201 imaging. Illustrated are two different forms of malalignment artifact that duplicate this patient's findings in a patient with normal perfusion."},
